{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/782763-hive-lair-trait","id":782763,"title":"Hive Lair Trait","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-09T06:33:43-08:00","id":782763,"title":"Hive Lair Trait","content":"I'm not sure I understand how Hive Lair Traits work. What if the Apex choose Earthquake? Would every lairs nearby be forced to continuously have earthquakes no matter what the players do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T06:37:35-08:00","id":782765,"title":"","content":"I think the apex trait has to be minor, and I'm approximately as confident that earthquake is major. That aside a beast can sever their lair from the hive if they want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T07:19:40-08:00","id":782784,"title":"","content":"There's no limit to the Apex trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T10:09:06-08:00","id":782893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/782763-hive-lair-trait#post782763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Apex choose Earthquake?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assumes a degree of in-character control and out-of-context decision-making that does not mesh with the narrative convention a Hive Trait is meant to represent.<br /> <br /> If the supernatural being with the highest level of nightmare-exposure in a population center is primarily known through the manifestation of earthquakes, some shit is going to go down soon enough, which is probably why most Hive Traits tend toward the lower-key.<br /> <br /> It's also kind of difficult to have a consistent feature running through the hive represented by an event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T16:45:37-08:00","id":783122,"title":"","content":"As for the chance of it being an earthquake I was imagining a place like California that's famous for earthquakes.<br /> <br /> But still, so was right in my interpretation that everything in the hive is permanently stuck with it and there is nothing the players can do without basically becoming the apex themselves? I'm not really sure how that is meant to be fun since it means any player that doesn't conform to the hive trait or leaves the hive is penalized. Even the minor traits being permanently on in every chamber would be annoying. I mean god, what if it was stench, there would barely be any beasts who Wouldn't leave that hive. Cramped would ruin so many horrors. Maze just leads to a giant amount of horrors who can't even figure a way through their own lair. Thunderous leaves horrors stuck permanently deaf. <br /> <br /> With the minor benefit of &quot;if your horror goes out looking for food, it might eat further away&quot; I don't see much reason why beasts would keep their lairs connected to the local hive. Just sounds like it ruins the point of horrors having lairs if the horror is constantly penalized while within them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T17:08:42-08:00","id":783135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/782763-hive-lair-trait?p=783122#post783122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But still, so was right in my interpretation that everything in the hive is permanently stuck with it and there is nothing the players can do without basically becoming the apex themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>You also have the options of developing the same Lair Trait or brooding up with the Apex or another Beast with the appropriate immunity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not really sure how that is meant to be fun since it means any player that doesn't conform to the hive trait or leaves the hive is penalized. Even the minor traits being permanently on in every chamber would be annoying. I mean god, what if it was stench, there would barely be any beasts who Wouldn't leave that hive. Cramped would ruin so many horrors. Maze just leads to a giant amount of horrors who can't even figure a way through their own lair. Thunderous leaves horrors stuck permanently deaf. </div> </div> </div>I'l be perfectly frank: this is a terrible reading premised on multiple deliberately disruptive assumptions and the way you're talking makes it sound like it would be a waste of time to attempt to remedy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T17:19:58-08:00","id":783142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/782763-hive-lair-trait?p=783135#post783135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also have the options of developing the same Lair Trait or brooding up with the Apex or another Beast with the appropriate immunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the brood immunity only works as part of you imposing the trait.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'l be perfectly frank: this is a terrible reading premised on multiple deliberately disruptive assumptions and the way you're talking makes it sound like it would be a waste of time to attempt to remedy it. </div> </div> </div>I sincerely do not know what you mean. It was not my intent to be deliberately disruptive. I simply do not understand why the game mechanic was made the way it is, when it seems like a large amount of the time it leaves horrors near-permanently penalized in the place that is meant to define them and be Their lair, so I intentionally thought my interpretation was likely flawed and sought to remedy that by asking in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T17:34:57-08:00","id":783153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/782763-hive-lair-trait?p=783142#post783142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that the brood immunity only works as part of you imposing the trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Apex granting a Beast immunity to the Hive Trait is specifically called out as the means by which characters besides the Apex can access any other Chamber in the hive or roam it to gain the benefits of expanded feeding grounds, brood Lairs with otherwise-incompatible Horrors and Lair Traits are a thing, and there's no specified expiration period on shared Environmental Immunity (and in fact assuming that there is one renders the chief effects of getting immunity from the Apex nonsensical).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I sincerely do not know what you mean. It was not my intent to be deliberately disruptive. </div> </div> </div>Treating Lair Traits as though they're inescapable always-on distributed sensory phenomena when the examples include &quot;a hive with a Makara Apex has a river running through its Chambers&quot; and there's a sidebar that's existed since the first draft elaborating that Lair Traits act more or less like the natural phenomena they resemble (which means there's plenty of plausible explanations for why a given Horror might not be bothered by, say, the Stench trait as manifested in a cloud of ammonia) is going directly against the intent of the material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I simply do not understand why the game mechanic was made the way it is, when it seems like a large amount of the time it leaves horrors near-permanently penalized in the place that is meant to define them and be Their lair, so I intentionally thought my interpretation was likely flawed and sought to remedy that by asking in this thread. </div> </div> </div>The premise that this element of a collaborative storytelling game that people are ostensibly playing for fun is problematic because <i>the people using it might deliberately pick a Hive Trait that ruins their game experience</i> is inherently flawed, particularly when the book goes out of its way to highlight the matter in its Storytelling chapter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Apex</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An important part of this step is determining the region\u2019s Apex. Remember that the Apex is often a Beast, but that\u2019s because Beasts often interact the most directly with the Primordial Dream. Any type of supernatural character can become an Apex; the position can shift, however, as another character becomes more relevant and powerful. If the Storyteller has an idea for the Apex, she can share it, otherwise, let the players figure it out. <b>Likewise, let them choose the Hive Trait that runs through the Chambers and Lairs in the area, and ask them how that Trait changes or works with their characters' Lairs.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-09-2015, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T18:38:34-08:00","id":783186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/782763-hive-lair-trait?p=783153#post783153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Apex granting a Beast immunity to the Hive Trait is specifically called out as the means by which characters besides the Apex can access any other Chamber in the hive or roam it to gain the benefits of expanded feeding grounds, brood Lairs with otherwise-incompatible Horrors and Lair Traits are a thing, and there's no specified expiration period on shared Environmental Immunity (and in fact assuming that there is one renders the chief effects of getting immunity from the Apex nonsensical).</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to see, thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The premise that this element of a collaborative storytelling game that people are ostensibly playing for fun is problematic because <i>the people using it might deliberately pick a Hive Trait that ruins their game experience</i> is inherently flawed </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about people deliberately picking Hive Traits to ruin someone's game experience, I mean, if I someone is doing that (player or storyteller) you'd probably stop playing with them.It just seemed as though many traits (like the ones I've mentioned) have issues when forced upon all chambers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T20:35:20-08:00","id":783217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/782763-hive-lair-trait?p=783186#post783186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't talking about people deliberately picking Hive Traits to ruin someone's game experience, I mean, if I someone is doing that (player or storyteller) you'd probably stop playing with them.It just seemed as though many traits (like the ones I've mentioned) have issues when forced upon all chambers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also was not talking about deliberately picking Hive Traits to ruin someone's gaming experience. I was saying that the odds that a group would deliberately pick a Hive Trait <i>that they are not prepared to work with or around</i> is incredibly unlikely.<br /> <br /> And again, in plain language so the message gets across: <b>Lair Traits are not necessarily Chamber-wide effects, and several of the ones that are still exist as part of discrete phenomena that largely adhere to rules that follow from their manifestations.</b> An Apex whose Hive Trait is Cramped isn't rendering every Chamber in the hive into a tunnel system, it's <i>attached a Cramped tunnel system to every Chamber in the Hive.</i> Thunderous doesn't mean every Chamber is deafening to be in, it means <i>there's a potential source of deafening noise that can reach every Chamber</i>. The Maze that Inoue applies to the hive of Tokyo does not mean all the Chambers are labyrinthine, it means <i>there is a labyrinth adjoining the entire hive.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T21:32:21-08:00","id":783230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/782763-hive-lair-trait?p=783217#post783217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also was not talking about deliberately picking Hive Traits to ruin someone's gaming experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said that &quot;The premise that this element of a collaborative storytelling game that people are ostensibly playing for fun is problematic because <i>the people using it might deliberately pick a Hive Trait that ruins their game experience</i> is inherently flawed&quot; and I was saying that was not my premise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was saying that the odds that a group would deliberately pick a Hive Trait <i>that they are not prepared to work with or around</i> is incredibly unlikely. </div> </div> </div>The group does not always have the apex as a member. I'd be surprised if the brood contained the Apex at the start of a standard beast game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And again, in plain language so the message gets across: <b>Lair Traits are not necessarily Chamber-wide effects, and several of the ones that are still exist as part of discrete phenomena that largely adhere to rules that follow from their manifestations.</b> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why you're being aggressive about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T21:36:42-08:00","id":783235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/782763-hive-lair-trait?p=783230#post783230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said that &quot;The premise that this element of a collaborative storytelling game that people are ostensibly playing for fun is problematic because <i>the people using it might deliberately pick a Hive Trait that ruins their game experience</i> is inherently flawed&quot; and I was saying that was not my premise.<br /> <br /> The group does not always have the apex as a member. I'd be surprised if the brood contained the Apex at the start of a standard beast game.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why you're being aggressive about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a long-established and thoroughly-ingrained lack of patience for failure-to-read.<br /> <br /> Read:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Apex</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An important part of this step is determining the region\u2019s Apex. Remember that the Apex is often a Beast, but that\u2019s because Beasts often interact the most directly with the Primordial Dream. Any type of supernatural character can become an Apex; the position can shift, however, as another character becomes more relevant and powerful. <b>If the Storyteller has an idea for the Apex, she can share it, otherwise, let the players figure it out. </b><b><b>Likewise, let them choose the Hive Trait that runs through the Chambers and Lairs in the area, and ask them how that </b>Trait changes or works with their characters' Lairs.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T23:15:02-08:00","id":783258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/782763-hive-lair-trait?p=783235#post783235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a long-established and thoroughly-ingrained lack of patience for failure-to-read.<br /> <br /> Read:</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, when I read what you quoted, I only read what you bolded since whenever anyone else does that, they are bolding the section you're meant to read and mistook that to be for when they are the Apex.<br /> <br /> But regardless, still no reason to be rude to someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}